  "facts": [
    "The Fréjus Road Tunnel, opened on 12 July 1980, stretches 13 km under Col du Fréjus, making it the longest road tunnel that crosses an international border and carrying 80% of commercial traffic between France and Italy.",
    "After the 1999 Mont Blanc fire, the Fréjus Tunnel adopted a strict 70 km/h speed limit, 150 m vehicle spacing, and 11 fire‑proof shelters, yet a 2005 blaze still claimed two Slovak lorry drivers.",
    "Construction of a second bore began in 2009, breaking through on 17 November 2014, and opened to traffic on 1 August 2025, adding an emergency lane while keeping the tunnel’s single‑lane capacity unchanged."
